    <statement><p>Consider the four functions graphed in the figure below, and assume the equations for <em>A, B, C,</em> and <em>D</em> can all be written in the form <m>y=ab^t</m>.</p>
<p>Which function has the smallest value for <m>b</m>?
<var form="popup">
<li>
<p>C</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>A</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>B</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>D</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>?</p>
</li>
</var></p>
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/sec-exp-functions-5-8-image-1.png" width="66%"/>
<p>(Click on graph to enlarge)</p>
</statement>
    <solution><alert>  SOLUTION </alert>



The function with the smallest <m>b</m> should be the one that is decreasing the fastest.  We note that <em> D </em> decreases faster than the others, so <em> D </em> has the smallest <m>b</m>.



</solution>
